  "quotations": [
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q01",
      "pdf_pages": [
        10
      ],
      "quote": "we also have to normalize return on capital, reinvestment and cost of financing",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q02",
      "pdf_pages": [
        11
      ],
      "quote": "we are double counting growth, once by normalizing earnings and again by using a higher growth rate.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q03",
      "pdf_pages": [
        14
      ],
      "quote": "the averaging should occur over a period long enough to cover an entire cycle.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q04",
      "pdf_pages": [
        14
      ],
      "quote": "we can average profit margins over time, instead of net profits",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q05",
      "pdf_pages": [
        14
      ],
      "quote": "apply the average profit margin to revenues in the most recent period to estimate normalized earnings.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q06",
      "pdf_pages": [
        14
      ],
      "quote": "by looking at ratios of revenue or book capital over time, rather than the absolute values.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q07",
      "pdf_pages": [
        15
      ],
      "quote": "this approach will also fail to incorporate the characteristics (operating efficiencies or inefficiencies) that may lead a firm to be different from the rest of the sector.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q08",
      "pdf_pages": [
        16
      ],
      "quote": "Averaging the pre-tax operating margin from 1998 to 2009 yields an average operating margin of 7.33%.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q09",
      "pdf_pages": [
        17
      ],
      "quote": "since neither the debt ratio nor the cost of capital has moved substantially over time, we will use this as the normalized cost of capital.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q10",
      "pdf_pages": [
        17
      ],
      "quote": "We will also assume that the firm will be able to generate a return on capital equal to its cost of capital on its investments.",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q11",
      "pdf_pages": [
        21
      ],
      "quote": "Return on capital = Operating Income (1-tax rate)/ Invested Capital",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q12",
      "pdf_pages": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "quote": "With reinvestment and cost of financing, it will require some subjective judgments",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CYC-Q13",
      "pdf_pages": [
        23
      ],
      "quote": "allow earnings to follow the current cycle for the short term",
      "comparison": "exact after whitespace normalization",
      "matched": true
    }
  ],
